in order to make the cisco phones WORK with the server, you need to add this snippet of code to the SEP XML file.

<authenticationURL>http://ALERT_SERVER_IP:8080/auth</authenticationURL>   <!-- inside <device> -->

<vendorConfig>
  <webAccess>0</webAccess>                                              <!-- 0 = web server on -->
</vendorConfig><authenticationURL>http://ALERT_SERVER_IP:8080/auth</authenticationURL>   <!-- inside <device> -->

<vendorConfig>
  <webAccess>0</webAccess>                                              <!-- 0 = web server on -->
</vendorConfig>

also, THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT!!!!

this ONLY works with cisco phones that support services AND a web server, it also might not work on cisco phones that run open SIP firmware
at the moment.
